window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>A magical talent show, a ghostly messenger and a devious murder.</p> <p></p> <p>Elsie’s problems are piling up faster than the ‘treasures’ in Zippy’s hoard…</p> <p></p> <p>On the night of the Obsidian Moon, everyone in town’s on edge.</p> <p></p> <p>It’s the one night of the year when ghosts can cross into the mortal realm—and believe me, they can hold a grudge.</p> <p></p> <p>But when a dead body washes up in the pond, the cause of death is ghastly rather than ghostly.</p> <p></p> <p>The victim is someone from Colt Ridgeback’s past… and part of the reason he lives in his mountain cabin, isolated from the warmth of the town.</p> <p></p> <p>When he’s named as a suspect, Elsie knows she has to clear his name—and bring him back into the fold.</p> <p></p> <p>But not even a murder is going to stop Professor Hissington’s Dragonsoul Academy’s Annual Talent Show.</p> <p></p> <p>Elsie doesn’t have a talent (unless slamming an entire dozen hazelnut cream donuts counts? If so, just give her the trophy already) but she has a magic wand, the power of the All-Flame and a dragon familiar. But a gathering of all the young dragonmancers together with their familiars is risky business.</p> <p></p> <p>It’s the kind of event that draws the eyes of the Obsidian Covenant…Elsie’s also drawn the attention of someone—or something—else.</p> <p></p> <p>A mysterious woman seems to know an awful lot about Elsie’s past, her family and her future.</p> <p></p> <p>She conjures up a frightening vision, and Elsie doesn’t know whether the images can be trusted, or if it’s all a trap.</p> <p></p> <p>Can Elsie clear Colt’s name (and unburden his guilty heart), perform in the talent show and decipher the clues about her birth family?</p> <p></p> <p>Or is this the time when everything is going to crash and burn…</p> <p></p> <p>This is a full-length paranormal cozy mystery novel with animals who won’t shut up, baby dragons too cute for their own good, magic spells for all of life’s little annoyances and a supernatural town hidden deep in the mountains in a land that time forgot.</p>"; 
